### Samble 2.x demo — the whole flow, in order.
### Run the server first: `npm run dev`.
### Two seeded users, both with password `demo1234`:
###   owner -> every permission (`*`)
###   staff -> can view users, and view/manage products
@host = http://localhost:16001

### The same flow from a browser, if you prefer clicking it:
###   http://localhost:16001/public/
### It is served by this application's own `static()`, so it is same-origin and
### the session cookie needs nothing argued about.

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 1. Anonymous
### `me` answers the anonymous: it reads `this.auth.optional`, not `.actor`.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### Reading products without signing in -> 401. The endpoint calls
### `this.auth.assert('catalog.products.view')`, and nobody is signed in.
GET {{host}}/api/products

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 2. Validation
### A body that fails class-validator -> 422, with the offending field named.
### Nothing in `main()` runs.
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 3. Sign in as staff
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "staff", "password": "demo1234" }

### Now `me` reports the actor and the permission keys it holds.
GET {{host}}/api/auth/me

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 4. Permissions
### staff may view and manage products. Note `badges` on each one: the seeded
### products have stock to spare, so the extension point answers nothing for
### them. Create the one below (stock 5) and a "Low stock" badge appears —
### contributed by `reports`, without catalog changing or knowing.
GET {{host}}/api/products

### ...and only enabled ones, filtered by query string (a STRING: 'true').
GET {{host}}/api/products?onlyEnabled=true

### 201, because the endpoint sets `this.httpStatus`.
POST {{host}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Router 4G", "stock": 5 }

### Two writes in one transaction: the product's stock and its movement.
### It also announces `catalog.product.restocked`, and `reports` prints a line from
### a module `catalog` knows nothing about — look at the server output.
POST {{host}}/api/products/1/restock
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 10 }

### An id that does not exist -> 404 thrown from `main()`, same error shape.
GET {{host}}/api/products/9999

### A non-numeric id -> 422 from the param DTO, before `main()` is reached.
GET {{host}}/api/products/abc

### staff CANNOT create users -> 403 (identity.users.manage).
### Note the difference with step 1: there it was 401. Signed in but not
### allowed is a different answer than not signed in at all.
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "new", "fullName": "New One", "password": "demo1234", "role": "staff" }

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 5. Sign in as owner
POST {{host}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "owner", "password": "demo1234" }

### Same request as above, now 201: owner holds `*`.
POST {{host}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "username": "new", "fullName": "New One", "password": "demo1234", "role": "staff" }

GET {{host}}/api/users

### ------------------------------------------------- 6. Answers that are not JSON
### A page: `main()` returns `view('products', ...)`, rendered from
### `catalog/views/products.pug`. Note the URL: it is NOT under /api, because
### the class says `@Module('products', { basePath: '/' })` — a page belongs
### where people link to it. `logs/router.log` shows where everything mounted.
GET {{host}}/products/page

### The same catalog as a spreadsheet: `main()` returns `csv(products, ...)`.
### Note the response headers — text/csv and a Content-Disposition with the
### accented filename sent twice, sanitized and as UTF-8.
GET {{host}}/api/products/export

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 7. A module shaped like an extension
### `reports` owns no table. It reads identity AND catalog through their
### contracts, without importing either, and answers under its own id because
### it declares no @Group.
GET {{host}}/api/reports/summary

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 8. Docs
### OpenAPI generated from the same decorators used for routing.
GET {{host}}/docs.json

### ---------------------------------------------------------------- 9. Sign out
POST {{host}}/api/auth/logout
